		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=4407#p4407"><![CDATA[
Is there a way to check collisions again against a single collision object?<br><br>It occurs to me that the way I'm resolving collisions could cause additional collisions. For example, if in a single time step an object collides with 2 other objects, resolving the second collision could cause another collision with the first object (which had already been resolved). Ideally, I'd like to resolve any collisions for a single object and then recheck it to make sure the resolution hasn't caused more collisions without checking for collisions in the whole world again. Is there a way to do this?<br><br>Thanks.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1757">btmorex</a> — Mon Jun 04, 2007 12:51 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
